{"text": " So that probably cost me in the neighborhood of probably $50 million. I'll tell you a quick story. I had a competitor that ended up taking a bunch of my top testimonials that we kind of converted to semi-employees because they were big evangelists back in the gym launch days. This guy was offering one-on-one coaching to help people out. I never did that. So they were cheaper. They were doing one-on-one and they had some of my top customers becoming advocates. My feathers got all ruffled and I was like, it's war time. We got to go to the mattresses. We got to really change the business up. And so I did this big relaunch internally to my existing customer base. I did this big value stack and I said, you're going to get all this extra stuff, not for the same price you're paying me, but for less. I took my existing recurring base and I reduced my revenue by $500,000 top line per month. I increased my costs and I took my top line down by $6 million. I then ended up selling that business, obviously, and the business never recovered that profit. And so that probably cost me in the neighborhood of probably $50 million. That competitor ended up killing that business because it wasn't fucking profitable. I was the market leader and someone came in to undercut me and then I said, oh, I'll copy the moron. You will never go out of business focusing on the customer. You just focus on the customer and you'll win.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 3.6, "text": " So that probably cost me in the neighborhood of probably $50 million.", "tokens": [50364, 407, 300, 1391, 2063, 385, 294, 264, 7630, 295, 1391, 1848, 2803, 2459, 13, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14108596049563984, "compression_ratio": 1.6677316293929711, "no_speech_prob": 0.019870858639478683}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 3.6, "end": 4.6000000000000005, "text": " I'll tell you a quick story.", "tokens": [50544, 286, 603, 980, 291, 257, 1702, 1657, 13, 50594], "temperature